{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_growth_trichotomy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_growth_trichotomy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Archimedean","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.bounded_condNumber_forces_beta_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.bounded_condNumber_forces_beta_zero","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L195-L231","doc":"**A bounded condition number forces `β = 0`.**  If `C_L` is bounded then no\npositive exponent survives `beta_lower`, because `κ^(β/2) → ∞` overtakes any\nbound.  This is the `.md`'s branch-(A) identification, derived rather than\nassumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_branches_exclusive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_branches_exclusive","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L178-L184","doc":"**Branches A and B are mutually exclusive.**  Stated honestly: the content is\n`(0 : ℝ) ≠ 1`, so the hypotheses are jointly unsatisfiable and no instance is\nconsulted.  It is kept because the `.md` asserts exclusivity, not because the\nstructure supplies it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_marginal_undetermined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_marginal_undetermined","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L173-L176","doc":"Structure-level form of `beta_marginal_undetermined`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_trichotomy_exhaustive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.levi_trichotomy_exhaustive","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L168-L171","doc":"Structure-level form of `beta_trichotomy`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.branchB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.branchB","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L166-L166","doc":"**Branch B:** `β = 1` (`C_L ~ κ`) ⇒ Levi degenerates (NS-regular). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.branchA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.branchA","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L164-L164","doc":"**Branch A:** `β = 0` (`C_L = O(1)`) ⇒ Levi non-degenerate (NS-singular). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.beta_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.beta_lower","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L161-L161","doc":"**…and it is attained:** for every `ε > 0`, `κ^(β-ε) ≤ C_L(κ)` for\ninfinitely many `κ`.  Upper and lower together say exactly\n`limsup_κ log C_L(κ) / log κ = β`; the upper bound alone would be satisfied\nby any exponent at least the true one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.beta_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.beta_upper","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L155-L155","doc":"**`beta` is an upper exponent for `condNumber`:** for every `ε > 0`,\n`C_L(κ) ≤ κ^(β+ε)` for all large `κ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.beta_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.beta_mem","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L152-L152","doc":"**Bounded-rate regime:** `0 ≤ β ≤ 1` (`C_L` grows no faster than `κ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.beta","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L150-L150","doc":"Growth exponent `β = limsup_κ log C_L(κ) / log κ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.condNumber_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.condNumber_pos","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L148-L148","doc":"A condition number is positive — without this `log C_L` is meaningless and\nthe exponent below is not about anything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.condNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.condNumber","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L145-L145","doc":"The Levi condition number `C_L(κ)` at ladder step `κ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy.mk","kind":"ctor","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L143-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LeviGrowthTrichotomy","kind":"structure","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L130-L166","doc":"Growth-rate data for the Levi condition number `C_L(κ)` along the\nroot-of-unity ladder `q_κ = e^{iπ/κ}`, refining `conj:levi-degeneracy`.\n\nThe proposition `leviNonDegenerate` — \"the Levi form is non-degenerate along\nthe ladder\", both eigenvalues positive — is a **parameter**: the branch\nfields are claims about a *given* non-degeneracy predicate, not about one the\ninstance is free to invent.\n\n`beta` is the growth exponent `limsup_κ log C_L(κ) / log κ`, and\n`beta_upper` / `beta_lower` are that `limsup` written out without `Filter`.\nThey are what makes `condNumber` load-bearing rather than decorative; see the\nfile docstring for the two instances that satisfied the previous definition\nwith no content at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.beta_marginal_undetermined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.beta_marginal_undetermined","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L118-L123","doc":"**The marginal window is a genuine third case.** When `0 < β < 1`, neither\n`β = 0` nor `β = 1` holds, so neither branch is triggered. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.beta_trichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.beta_trichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/levi_growth_trichotomy.lean#L105-L116","doc":"**The trichotomy is exhaustive on `[0, 1]`.** Every bounded-rate exponent\nfalls into one of `β = 0`, `0 < β < 1`, `β = 1` — so the original two-branch\ndichotomy (`β = 0` xor `β = 1`) is *not* a valid partition; the marginal\nwindow `0 < β < 1` is the missing third case. ","signatureChunk":0}]}